issue_comments.body:
@noooop, addressed [the pooling request](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/58660#issuecomment-6307936012) in `4f0d282288` and pushed it.

Embedding and generic pooling now use `create_json_response()`; `get_json_response_cls()` is removed. The existing ndarray fast path, base64 encoding, Cohere `exclude_none`, plugin payloads and binary streaming are preserved. I also updated `load_aware_call` to attach completion accounting to plain `Response`, so moving these routes to the helper does not decrement load before the body is sent.

Latest validation: **135 unit tests** and **18 in-process ASGI checks** passed, including pooling/embedding/Cohere float/base64/binary responses and load accounting. All applicable pre-commit hooks passed. The PR description includes NumPy timings and the exact validation scope. Model-backed/GPU reruns remain unavailable; these were agent-run checks with stub engine outputs for ASGI.
